Files: media/theme_47-trimmed.mp4
Copyright: XIGMATEK (the panel's vendor); this file is that vendor's footage with
 its first 17 frames removed - a cut of their clip, not a copy of it, and the
 holder has granted no licence for either
License: OTHER
 This one file in `media/` is not byte-for-byte anything, and it is called out
 separately for that reason. `theme_47.mp4`, the vendor's, opens on 17 still
 frames (0.85 s at 20 fps) with a play button burned into the middle of the
 picture; a drawn overlay placed under those frames shows the button, so the head
 was removed - 168 frames / 8.40 s / 1 071 306 B taken from 185 / 9.25 s /
 1 211 106 B, re-encoded, no crop, no scaling, no colour change, nothing else
 touched. It is the background `birdseye` pairs with, and it ships in the code
 package because a theme that names a backdrop the package does not carry draws
 its readings over whatever the panel happens to store.
 .
 Modifying someone's footage is a different act from copying it, so the assessment
 is stated here rather than inherited from the paragraph below: the same
 interoperability-and-record-keeping grounds, the same offer to take the file down
 if the rights holder says otherwise, and no claim that the result is GPL. The
 original's digest is verified against the library manifest by
 tests/test_birdseye.py, which is what keeps "we copied it and cut it, we did not
 edit it" a check instead of a sentence.

