License: GPL-3.0-or-later+OTHER
 The two names in that one field are the two halves of the file it applies to.
 The drawing on top is ours, under GPL-3.0-or-later as the paragraph of that
 name below says.  What sits under it is one frame lifted out of a XIGMATEK
 background clip, and the vendor has granted no licence for it, so the
 combination is redistributed on the same assessment the OTHER paragraph
 below states - interoperability and record-keeping, with the offer to take
 the files down if the rights holder says otherwise.  A file under that Files
 stanza is therefore not clean to relicense: GPL covers our contribution and
 nothing else.

License: OTHER
 What was done, plainly: the files under themes/alpha/ and the three clips in
 media/ named above (`Theme_11.mp4`, `Theme_25.mp4`, `theme_48.mp4`) were copied,
 byte for byte, out of a vendor installation on the author's
 bench machine (`C:\Program Files\ALPHA\`, reached from Linux as a mounted
 Windows volume; themes/alpha/README.md names the paths and the tool,
 tools/thm_unlock.py, that took them out).  The `.thm` theme files were decrypted
 with constants read out of the vendor application's own compiled code, in order
 to learn what the panel is being told to draw.  Those containers were carried in
 the 0.1 and 0.2 releases and are not redistributed from 0.3: what is kept of them
 here is their byte count and sha256, in manifest.json, beside the vendor path
 where they come from - the vendor's own installer, named in themes/alpha/.
 .
 No permission to copy them was asked for and none was given, so no licence for
 them is claimed here: they are redistributed as an act of interoperability and
 record-keeping, on the assessment that documenting an undocumented, unlicensed
 USB protocol and reproducing the assets it consumes is within fair use for that
 purpose.  They are separated into their own binary package
 (xigmatek-connect-lcd-themes), and nothing in this project needs them to run:
 removing that package takes them away and leaves the display working.
 .
 If the rights holder considers this wrong, say so to the address in
 Upstream-Contact and the files come down; that offer is in README.md as well.
 Xigmatek, Connect and ALPHA are the rights holder's names, and nothing here is
 affiliated with, endorsed by or approved by XIGMATEK.
